00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:30.040
Stop calling me.
别再给我打电话了。

151
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.400
Tell people to stop calling us.
告诉大家别再打给我们了。

152
00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

153
00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.300
There was a scene that let up before she ruined your painting.
原本有个场景是在她毁掉你的画之前发生的。

154
00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:38.700
I'm going to save it.
我打算把它留着。

155
00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.180
I'm going to share it when it would have happened in the episode, okay?
我打算在剧集里原本该出现的时候把它放出来，好吗？

156
00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:41.820
Okay.
好的。

157
00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.520
That sort of set up why she even started cleaning it in the first place.
那段戏交代了她为什么一开始会去清理那幅画。

158
00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:46.880
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

159
00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:47.620
Yeah.
是啊。

160
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.060
But I think it will make more sense if I bring it up where it would have occurred.
但我觉得如果把它放回原本该出现的地方，逻辑会更通顺。

161
00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.180
I like it.
我喜欢这个主意。

162
00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:58.760
After we read the script in our table read, which is the week before we're meant to shoot it,
在我们进行剧本围读之后，也就是正式拍摄前的一周，

163
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:05.660
I, like, as soon as I started reading it, I got hot inside, you know?
我，就像，我一读到那段，整个人就火冒三丈，你知道吗？

164
00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:10.800
Like, you heat up, and I could barely focus on the rest of the table read.
就是那种气血上涌的感觉，我几乎没法集中精力读完剩下的剧本。

165
00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.420
You had a physical reaction.
你产生了生理反应。

166
00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:12.960
I did.
没错。

167
00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.180
You, like, flushed.
你，就像，脸红了。

168
00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.280
Like, your cheeks were red.
你的脸颊都红了。

169
00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:15.800
Yes!
是的！

170
00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.860
I waited until after the table read.
我一直等到围读结束。

171
00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:19.800
Everybody left.
大家都走了。

172
00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:20.880
And this was unusual.
这很不寻常。

173
00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:25.740
I did not normally stay after a table read and, like, give my feelings.
我通常不会在围读结束后留下来，去表达我的感受。

174
00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:27.100
No, no.
不，不会。

175
00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:30.880
No, in fact, we usually had to scooch out because we had to go to hair and makeup to get back to set.
事实上，我们通常得赶紧溜，因为得去化妆间做造型，然后回片场。

176
00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:32.660
Yeah, to go back to shoot.
对，回去接着拍。

177
00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:36.720
But I was like, listen, you cannot destroy Pam's painting.
但我当时说，听着，你们不能毁掉帕姆的画。

178
00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:37.700
You can't do it.
你们不能这么做。

179
00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:39.500
It's the heartbeat of the show.
那是这部剧的灵魂所在。

180
00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.840
It's on the wall.
它挂在墙上。

181
00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.740
It's her relationship with Michael.
那是她和迈克尔之间关系的象征。

182
00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.260
It's hope.
那是希望。

183
00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:45.600
It's so many things.
它代表了太多东西。

184
00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:46.440
Like, you don't understand.
你们根本不明白。

185
00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.380
Like, you can't make this a gag.
你们不能把它当成一个笑料。

186
00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.460
And Paul Lieberstein was like, I think it's funny.
保罗·利伯斯坦当时说，我觉得这很有趣。

187
00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:53.780
What are you talking about?
你在说什么啊？

188
00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.700
And it was a battle.
那真是一场抗争。

189
00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:56.700
I was like, no, no, no.
我当时说，不，不，不。

190
00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.020
You don't understand.
你们不明白。

191
00:08:58.360 --> 00:08:59.840
Like, you cannot do it.
你们不能这么做。

192
00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.180
And I called Greg.
我还给格雷格打了电话。

193
00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.320
I, like, made my case to anyone who would listen.
我向每一个愿意听的人陈述我的理由。

194
00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.000
They shot it anyway.
但他们还是拍了。

195
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:07.980
They were like, I'm sorry.
他们说，抱歉。

196
00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:08.840
It's staying in.
这部分得保留。

197
00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.080
We really like this gag.
我们真的很喜欢这个笑料。

198
00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.240
We think it's great.
我们觉得它很棒。

199
00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.800
We like it.
我们喜欢它。

200
00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:13.440
Oh, they were so wrong.
哦，他们真是大错特错。

201
00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:14.700
They were so wrong.
他们大错特错了。

202
00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:19.960
Lady, after we shot it, I went into the edit bay.
女士，我们拍完之后，我进了剪辑室。

203
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.080
And I was like, you have to take this out.
当时我就说，你们必须把这段删掉。

204
00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.280
You have to take this out.
你们必须把它删掉。

205
00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.260
I appealed to Dave Rogers.
我向戴夫·罗杰斯求情。

206
00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.660
I appealed to Brent Forrester.
我向布伦特·福雷斯特求情。

207
00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.460
Like, I would not shut up about it.
我简直没完没了地念叨这件事。

208
00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:32.140
Finally, in the end, they took it out.
最后，他们终于把它删掉了。

209
00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:33.660
They took it out.
他们把它删掉了。

210
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.580
And I was so relieved.
我当时如释重负。

211
00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:39.880
But you'll see next week, there's not Pam's watercolor on the wall.
但下周你们会发现，墙上没有帕姆的水彩画了。

212
00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.180
Because that was the week they were editing and still deciding.
因为那是他们正在剪辑、还在犹豫的那一周。

213
00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.740
So if you look, Pam's watercolor is missing for a couple of episodes.
所以如果你仔细看，帕姆的水彩画在几集里都消失了。

214
00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:52.400
And we just sneakily put it back on the wall without saying anything.
然后我们悄悄地把它放回墙上，什么也没说。

215
00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:53.860
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

216
00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:58.240
So for those episodes, there's no painting because you were still pleading your case.
所以在那几集里，画不见了，因为你当时还在据理力争。

217
00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.060
Yes.
没错。

218
00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:00.980
But I would not give up.
但我绝不放弃。

219
00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.540
And then, I mean, listen.
而且，我是说，听着。

220
00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:08.260
And the whole series ends on Pam's watercolor.
整个剧集最后是以帕姆的水彩画结尾的。

221
00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.100
I know.
我知道。

222
00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.580
And I couldn't imagine it ending any other way.
我无法想象还有什么比这更好的结局。

223
00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.660
I mean, that made me bawl my eyes out.
我是说，那让我哭得稀里哗啦。

224
00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:14.540
I know.
我知道。

225
00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:20.900
And you better believe that I marched right up to Paul Lieberstein when I read that ending
你最好相信，当我读到大结局的剧本时，我直接走到保罗·利伯斯坦面前，

226
00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:21.600
of the finale.
关于大结局的部分。

227
00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.500
And I was like, Paul, do you see now why Aaron couldn't destroy the watercolor?
我对他说，保罗，现在你明白为什么亚伦不能毁掉那幅水彩画了吧？

228
00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:28.720
Do you see?
你明白了吗？

229
00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.160
You held on to that for years.
你坚持了这么多年。

230
00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:31.820
Yes.
是的。

231
00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:39.400
Well, I'm so glad you did because it represents such a tender moment between Michael and Pam.
好吧，我真高兴你坚持住了，因为它代表了迈克尔和帕姆之间如此温柔的时刻。

232
00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.800
And it is the hope.
它就是希望。

233
00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:41.860
It's hope.
它是希望。

234
00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.260
It's hope in a frame.
它是画框里的希望。

235
00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:45.420
It's hope in a frame.
它是画框里的希望。

236
00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.080
I wish I'd said that.
真希望这话是我说的。

237
00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:48.600
It's hope in a frame.
它是画框里的希望。

238
00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.280
You're welcome.
不客气。

239
00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.740
Oh, man.
天哪。

240
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.700
Well, I'm really glad you fought hard for it.
好吧，我真的很庆幸你为它据理力争。

241
00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.940
I knew you didn't want it to be destroyed.
我知道你不想让它被毁掉。

242
00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.100
I remembered all of that.
我记得所有这些。

243
00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:00.260
I did not remember how hard you had to fight for it.
但我没记住你为了保住它付出了多少努力。

244
00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:01.140
Yeah.
是啊。

245
00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:05.520
I mean, there were two things in the series that I fought hard for.
我是说，剧集里有两件事是我极力争取过的。

246
00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:10.620
I would consistently fight that there be no infidelity in Jim and Pam's relationship.
我一直坚持吉姆和帕姆的感情中不能有不忠。

247
00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.840
That would often get brought up.
这事经常被提出来。

248
00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:16.920
And John and I would go say, no, no, no, no, no, no.
我和约翰就会去说，不，不，不，不，不，不。

249
00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:18.620
And this was the other thing.
而这就是另一件事。

250
00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:19.940
Don't destroy the painting.
别毁掉那幅画。

251
00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:20.740
Yeah.
没错。

252
00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:25.740
Well, Jenna, the amazing Randy Cordray shared with us that the whole destroying of Pam's
嗯，珍娜，了不起的兰迪·科德雷和我们分享说，毁掉帕姆那幅画的过程

253
00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:28.640
painting was considered a mini-stunt.
被视为一个小型的特技拍摄。

254
00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:29.680
Oh.
噢。

255
00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.380
Here's how they had to do it.
以下是他们必须采取的操作方式。

256
00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:36.220
Our special effects coordinator, Mike Thompson, created what the special effects folks call
我们的特效协调员迈克·汤普森制作了特效人员所说的

257
00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:37.940
an A-B reaction.
A-B反应。

258
00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:43.820
It's where two different substances are inert and non-reactive until mixed together.
这是一种两种不同物质在混合前呈惰性且无反应的状态。

259
00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.260
Oh, I remember that from chemistry class.
噢，我记得化学课上讲过这个。

260
00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.740
I was going to say, you didn't know we were going to have a little bit of science today.
我正想说呢，你没想到我们今天还会来点科学知识吧。

261
00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:52.740
The A substance was pre-applied over the watercolor.
A物质被预先涂抹在水彩画上。

262
00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.540
It dried clear and was not visible.
它干了之后是透明的，肉眼看不见。

263
00:11:55.940 --> 00:12:02.140
The B substance, a reactive, also clear liquid, was what Aaron sprayed.
B物质是一种同样透明的反应液体，就是亚伦喷洒的那种。

264
00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:08.800
There were minute openings in the top of the frame to allow the B liquid to run inside
画框顶部有微小的开口，可以让B液体流进

265
00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:09.600
the glass.
玻璃里面。

266
00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:15.000
And when the B chemical reacted with the A, it changed the colors and achieved the desired
当B化学物质与A发生反应时，它改变了颜色，达到了

267
00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.740
result of the gag, which was the watercolor's melting.
这个恶作剧预期的效果，也就是水彩画的“融化”。

268
00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:22.460
He even sent us a video of their practice run, which we can put in stories.
他甚至给我们发了一段他们练习时的视频，我们可以发到快拍里。

269
00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:27.620
Oh, then so people can see the melting of the watercolor.
噢，这样大家就能看到水彩画融化的过程了。

270
00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:28.340
Yes.
是的。

271
00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:29.180
Wow.
哇。

272
00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.700
But I thought that was so interesting.
我觉得这太有意思了。

273
00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:31.940
Look what all they had to do.
看看他们为了实现这一幕得做多少准备。

274
00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:36.680
To make this moment happen, I mean, ultimately, I'm glad it didn't make it in the show, right?
我是说，归根结底，我很高兴它最终没出现在正片里，对吧？

275
00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.920
But pretty cool to see what all they had to do.
但能看到他们为了实现效果所做的一切还是很酷的。

276
00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:46.260
Gosh, it's sort of like a very mini version of everything Randy was doing to get a horse
天哪，这就像是兰迪为了让马匹

277
00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:47.660
to go over Niagara Falls.
翻越尼亚加拉大瀑布所做的一切的微缩版。

278
00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:48.580
Oh, no.
噢，不。

279
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.180
You know, like, how do I make this happen?
你知道，就像是“我该怎么实现这个效果呢？”

280
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.640
And then, oh, we actually cut it out of the episode.
然后，噢，我们实际上把它从剧集中剪掉了。

281
00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:53.960
Right.
没错。

282
00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:55.880
All right.
好了。

283
00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:01.640
Well, fast fact number three, we have a very big guest star this week.
那么，第三个速览事实，我们这周有一位非常大牌的客串明星。

284
00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.540
Mike Starr as Angelo Grotti.
饰演安杰洛·格罗蒂的迈克·斯塔尔。

285
00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:08.280
You guys might remember him from Dumb and Dumber.
你们可能还记得他在《阿呆与阿瓜》里的表演。

286
00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.940
He had a scene-stealing role.
他当时的角色非常抢戏。

287
00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:10.460
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

288
00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:14.960
He has been on Chicago Fire, The Young and the Restless, Ed.
他出演过《芝加哥烈焰》、《年轻和骚动不安的一族》以及《艾德》。

289
00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.620
He was so great.
他太棒了。

290
00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:17.880
He was the nicest man.
他是个非常好的人。

291
00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:19.120
So nice.
人特别好。

292
00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.640
And he's just been in everything, you guys.
而且他真的演过各种角色，伙计们。

293
00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:22.300
Everything.
各种角色。

294
00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:24.020
He's a total pro.
他是个十足的专业人士。

295
00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.200
I found this interview he did, and it was so cool.
我找到了他做过的一次采访，非常酷。

296
00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:33.180
He grew up in Queens, in Flushing, right near Shea Stadium, which is by where the Mets play.
他在皇后区的法拉盛长大，就在谢伊体育场附近，也就是大都会队主场那边。

297
00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.280
But in the interview, he said he was a Giants fan.
但在采访中，他说他是巨人队的球迷。

298
00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:37.600
He's married and has two kids.
他已婚，有两个孩子。

299
00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:38.940
His wife is a surgeon.
他的妻子是一名外科医生。

300
00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:44.080
And he kept his family in New York, and he would travel to be an actor.
他让家人留在纽约，自己则奔波各地去当演员。

301
00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:52.840
He just got bit by the acting bug and created this life as a working actor, but also raising
他刚迷上演戏，就此开启了职业演员的生活，同时还要在

302
00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:54.400
his family on the East CoaSt.
东海岸抚养他的家人。

303
00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:57.160
And he said he just goes where the work takes him.
他说他只是哪里有工作就去哪里。

304
00:13:57.420 --> 00:13:58.480
And I don't know.
我不知道。

305
00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.840
It just sounded so cool.
听起来太酷了。

306
00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:06.080
Again, another example of how lucky we were as a show to get these amazing, amazing actors.
这又是一个例子，说明我们这部剧有多幸运，能请到这些了不起的演员。

307
00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.240
Well, that's all I got, lady.
好吧，我就这些了，女士。

308
00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:12.280
Well, I have something from my Kinsey digital clutter.
嗯，我从我的金赛数字杂物里翻出了一些东西。

309
00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.320
Oh, these are my favorite segments.
哦，这是我最喜欢的环节。

310
00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.300
I'm telling you, I think I need a sting that's like,
